    <bpmn:process id="W_W5560" name="W5560. Informal-Settler Invasion &amp; Illegal Occupation of Banked Land — Detection, Relocation &amp; Ejection Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Detection of new informal-settler structures, illegal occupants, or third-party possession claims on a banked (pre-development) BuildRight landholding — caretaker report, geotagged patrol or drone imagery, real-property-tax inspection, barangay/LGU notice, or a buyer/lessee appearing with documents executed by a fake attorney-in-fact
Frequency: A recurring Philippine landbanking hazard: expect a handful of new occupation events per year across the banked portfolio, clustered where banked lots adjoin urbanizing barangays — rising with every year a parcel is held pre-development
Volume: 1 event × the occupied parcel (banked lots held 3–10 years ahead of the 10–15 store openings/year pipeline) × the occupant group (a few families to syndicate-scale settlements) × the resolution surface (barangay, LGU relocation track, courts, and where agrarian-adjacent, the DAR machinery)
Owner: Land Acquisition Specialist
Participants: Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate (portfolio decisions), Legal Counsel (VS-100 ejectment and title actions), Geodetic Engineer (the W5133 survey class), the caretaker network, Barangay &amp; LGU officials (relocation and social welfare), PNP (syndicate and fake-deed cases), Corporate Security (VS-159 site-hardening and intelligence), Tax Accountant (W5131 RPT continuity)
Source: workflow W5560 — Informal-Settler Invasion &amp; Illegal Occupation of Banked Land — Detection, Relocation &amp; Ejection Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5560_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5560_Lane1" name="Land Acquisition Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5560_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5560_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5560_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5560_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5560_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5560_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5560_Lane2" name="Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5560_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5560_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5560_Lane3" name="Facilities">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5560_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5560_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5560_Start5" name="Detection of new informal-settler structures, illegal occupants, or third-party…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5560_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5560_Task6" name="Evidence-first documentation within 72 hours">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Evidence-first documentation within 72 hours: geotagged photos, structure census, occupant headcount, drone imagery where flown, and a dated occupation log opened — the foundation of every later legal action and the prescription-interruption record
Responsible (R): Land Acquisition Specialist / Caretaker
Accountable (A): Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate
Duration: 3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5560_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5560_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5560_Task7" name="Classification &amp; strategy call">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Classification &amp; strategy call: genuine informal settlers (negotiation-led) vs professional-squatter syndicates (law-enforcement-led, RA 7279) vs the caretaker-fraud variant (internal investigation with VS-159/VS-100; fake-deed cases prosecuted); strategy recorded with rationale
Responsible (R): Land Acquisition Specialist / Legal
Accountable (A): Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5560_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5560_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5560_Task8" name="No-self-help discipline">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: No-self-help discipline: no fencing-people-out, demolition, or blocking of entry except through counsel-directed legal process; interim measures (signage, boundary marking) only with Legal sign-off — always
Responsible (R): Legal / Land Acquisition Specialist
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: Standing rule</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5560_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5560_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5560_Task9" name="Barangay &amp; LGU engagement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Barangay &amp; LGU engagement: barangay certification of the occupation; the LGU relocation and social-welfare track (UDHA&#x27;s relocation duty for qualified beneficiaries); negotiated relocation assistance assessed against the litigation alternative — the assessment documented either way
Responsible (R): Land Acquisition Specialist / Legal
Accountable (A): Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate
Duration: 1–3 months</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5560_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5560_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5560_Task10" name="Legal action">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Legal action: Rule 70 ejectment (forcible entry within one year of entry; unlawful detainer thereafter) via VS-100; injunction against syndicate leaders; criminal complaints for estafa/falsification where fake documents surface
Responsible (R): Legal / External Counsel
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 6–24 months</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5560_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5560_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5560_Task11" name="Site protection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Site protection: perimeter fencing to the W5150 standard, signage, caretaker re-vetting and rotation, geotagged patrol cadence tiered to the occupation risk; gate and access control
Responsible (R): Facilities / Corporate Security
Accountable (A): Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate
Duration: 2–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5560_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5560_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5560_Task12" name="Portfolio watch">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Portfolio watch: every banked lot risk-tiered and inspected on cadence; RPT declarations kept current per W5131 (tax continuity as possession and title hygiene); title monitoring refresh per W5130
Responsible (R): Land Acquisition Specialist / Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5560_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5560_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5560_Task13" name="Records &amp; intelligence">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Records &amp; intelligence: occupation log, resolution cost-and-duration register, and the syndicate modus file to VS-159; a development-schedule flag where occupation risk argues accelerating handover (the W5152 chain)
Responsible (R): Land Acquisition Specialist
Accountable (A): Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5560_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5560_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5560_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5560_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-141 (ensure land title &amp; acquisition due diligence) | - CTL-764 (ensure controlled execution — Land Feasibility, Site Acquisition &amp; Title Consolidation (PA-178.1).) | - operational: no eviction action without counsel sign-off; occupation evidence captured within 72 hours of detection; caretaker re-vetting annually; RPT continuity maintained on all banked parcels
Owner: Land Acquisition Specialist</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
